# UI test: an `implements` block that does not implement one of the interface's
# methods (SC0539).
#
# `conform`'s §1: the subject is the *block*, which named an interface and did
# not finish. `render` is written, `width` is not, and `width` has no body on
# the interface — so it is a requirement rather than a default, which is the
# distinction the first note draws.
#
# `preview` is here to prove the other half in the same file: it is declared
# *with* a body, so the block is under no obligation to restate it and nothing
# is reported about it. A rule that could not tell the two apart would report
# twice here and would be wrong once.

interface Render:
    def render(self) -> String
    def width(self) -> Int

    def preview(self) -> String:
        self.render()

type Doc:
    title: String

Doc implements Render:
    def render(self) -> String:
        String.new()
